{{!< default}}

{{!-- One tag's archive: a Feed filtered to a single tag.

Distinct from the Tags Directory, which lists tags rather than posts — the two look alike in the
card layout, and conflating them is exactly the ambiguity CONTEXT.md was written to settle. This
Surface pages through posts; that one lists subjects and does not.

The layout picker is `@custom.feed_layout`, the same select the Feed reads, because a buyer who
asked for a wide row per post meant it wherever posts are listed. It is read here and handed to
tag/surface.hbs as `layout`, the pattern home.hbs documents, and no partial below reads @custom.

`posts` and `pagination` are this channel's own: Ghost resolves how many rows a page holds in the
routing layer, from `posts_per_page` in this theme's package.json or from `limit:` on the route
in the publication's routes.yaml. Nothing here decides it. --}}

{{> "chrome/header"}}

<main
	id="main"
	class="grow"
	data-surface="tag"
	data-layout="{{#match @custom.feed_layout "Grid"}}Grid{{else}}List{{/match}}">

	{{> "tag/surface" layout=@custom.feed_layout}}

</main>

{{> "chrome/footer"}}
